    skos:definition "(2) A review under subsection (1) must have regard to the following matters:  (a) the state of competition in telecommunications markets;  Operational separation of Telstra  Schedule 11  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005 No. 119, 2005            29  (b) whether Telstra has a substantial degree of power in any telecommunications market;  (c) technological developments that have, or might reasonably be expected to have, a significant impact on competition in telecommunications markets;  (d) Telstra’s commercial incentives for supplying wholesale eligible services;  (e) costs and benefits of the operation of Part 8 of Schedule 1."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "47d55131895950b78462019ac3fd76a3e6c8dfb81052935caaea246c2dae93bd" ;
