concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-50a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "50A Designated services"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-11-sec-50a ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a designated service is an eligible service specified in a written determination made by the Minister under this subclause.  (2) The Minister must not make a determination under subclause (1) that specifies a service that is not an active declared service (within the meaning of section 152AR of the Trade Practices Act 1974) unless:  (a) the determination is the first determination made under subclause (1); or  (b) Telstra has given written consent to the making of the determination.  (3) Subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 applies to a power conferred on the Minister by subclause (1), but it applies with the change set out in subclause (4).  Schedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra" ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a designated service is an eligible service specified in a written determination made by the Minister under this subclause.  (2) The Minister must not make a determination under subclause (1) that specifies a service that is not an active declared service (within the meaning of section 152AR of the Trade Practices Act 1974) unless:  (a) the determination is the first determination made under subclause (1); or  (b) Telstra has given written consent to the making of the determination.  (3) Subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 applies to a power conferred on the Minister by subclause (1), but it applies with the change set out in subclause (4).  Schedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a092ed35717b4d7b229ad8cc02fc003b76bb2af42759c88d1eaf0ea63cb0f586" ;
    cof:pageNumber "39"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-50a-ss-1 ;
