concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-2005-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2005 No. 119, 2005"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-11-sec-2005-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The Minister must not vary a determination under subclause (1) so as to specify a service that is not an active declared service (within the meaning of section 152AR of the Trade Practices Act 1974) unless Telstra has given written consent to the variation of the determination.  (5) Before making a determination under subclause (1), the Minister must consult Telstra.  (6) A determination under subclause (1) is a legislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The Minister must not vary a determination under subclause (1) so as to specify a service that is not an active declared service (within the meaning of section 152AR of the Trade Practices Act 1974) unless Telstra has given written consent to the variation of the determination.  (5) Before making a determination under subclause (1), the Minister must consult Telstra.  (6) A determination under subclause (1) is a legislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "abede016a137789154f55284497fe4d85d28091f8387f37fd6cb73bcf1b8a9da" ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer ;
