concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-55 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "55 Effect of approval"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-11-sec-55 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Minister approves a draft operational separation plan, the plan becomes a final operational separation plan. The final operational separation plan comes into force at the time when Telstra is notified of the approval.  (2) A final operational separation plan is not a legislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003.  (3) Compliance with a final operational separation plan is not a condition of Telstra’s carrier licence." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the Minister approves a draft operational separation plan, the plan becomes a final operational separation plan. The final operational separation plan comes into force at the time when Telstra is notified of the approval.  (2) A final operational separation plan is not a legislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003.  (3) Compliance with a final operational separation plan is not a condition of Telstra’s carrier licence."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "38468480ab37c4bf489820be3c7ace5fba15a2811e45d7e3a20c754f5bd02c59" ;
    cof:pageNumber "43"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-55-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-55-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-55-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
