concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-60 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "60 Draft rectification plan to be given to Minister"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-11-sec-60 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This clause applies if Telstra has contravened, or is contravening, a final operational separation plan.  (2) The Minister may give Telstra a written direction requiring Telstra to give the Minister a draft rectification plan that relates to that contravention.  (3) Telstra must comply with the direction within 90 days after the day on which the direction was given.  Operational separation of Telstra  Schedule 11  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005 No. 119, 2005            43  (4) A direction under this clause is a legislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This clause applies if Telstra has contravened, or is contravening, a final operational separation plan.  (2) The Minister may give Telstra a written direction requiring Telstra to give the Minister a draft rectification plan that relates to that contravention.  (3) Telstra must comply with the direction within 90 days after the day on which the direction was given.  Operational separation of Telstra  Schedule 11  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005 No. 119, 2005            43  (4) A direction under this clause is a legislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9b256a2336a731f5a748a5653ffd267309fd7c079c2b7ed44b5e92a9ea6aa564" ;
