concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-61-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "61(3) Approval of draft by Minister"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-11-sec-61-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) In deciding whether to approve the plan, the Minister must have regard to the following matters:  (a) the extent to which the action proposed to be taken by Telstra is likely to ensure that:  (i) the contravention ceases; and  (ii) there is no repetition of the contravention in the future;  (b) such other matters (if any) as are specified in a written determination made by the Minister under this paragraph." ;
    skos:definition "(3) In deciding whether to approve the plan, the Minister must have regard to the following matters:  (a) the extent to which the action proposed to be taken by Telstra is likely to ensure that:  (i) the contravention ceases; and  (ii) there is no repetition of the contravention in the future;  (b) such other matters (if any) as are specified in a written determination made by the Minister under this paragraph."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f9232f155c8d9b72b477005816aaefac536356627e19abca26945922e6d6996c" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-61 ;
    cof:pageNumber "47"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Minister must consider certain matters when deciding to approve a plan." ;
