concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-64 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "64 Minister may direct Telstra to vary final rectification plan"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-11-sec-64 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This clause applies if a final rectification plan is in force.  (2) The Minister may, by written notice given to Telstra, direct Telstra to:  (a) prepare a draft variation of the plan in accordance with the direction; and  (b) give the draft variation to the Minister under subclause 63(1). The draft variation must be given to the Minister within 60 days after the day on which the direction was given.  (3) A direction under this clause is a legislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This clause applies if a final rectification plan is in force.  (2) The Minister may, by written notice given to Telstra, direct Telstra to:  (a) prepare a draft variation of the plan in accordance with the direction; and  (b) give the draft variation to the Minister under subclause 63(1). The draft variation must be given to the Minister within 60 days after the day on which the direction was given.  (3) A direction under this clause is a legislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7959c94107a331f5b2c0f6beebb8c3c3daf5d6a8b9fa5bd1f470966033166980" ;
    cof:pageNumber "49"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-64-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-64-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-64-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.49" .
doc:sch-11-sec-64 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "64 Minister may direct Telstra to vary final rectification plan" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This clause applies if a final rectification plan is in force.  (2) The Minister may, by written notice given to Telstra, direct Telstra to:  (a) prepare a draft variation of the plan in accordance with the direction; and  (b) give the draft variation to the Minister under subclause 63(1). The draft variation must be given to the Minister within 60 days after the day on which the direction was given.  (3) A direction under this clause is a legislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003." ;
    cof:pageNumber "49"^^xsd:integer .

